  "user_request_original": "Design a 22-layer alternating multilayer infrared filter on CaF2 (Daimon-20) substrate for dual-band transmission. Stack sequence from air ambient: ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2 (22 layers total). Optimize individual layer thicknesses with two-tier perturbation: layers 1-12 constrained to ±3% variation around baseline thicknesses of 478.0 nm (ZnS) and 815.0 nm (MgF2) alternating; layers 13-22 allowed ±12% independent variation. Spectral range 3500-5300 nm. Target: maximize mean transmittance in passbands 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm; minimize mean transmittance in stopbands 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm. Normal incidence, coherent thin-film calculation. No metal layers. Materials resolved from registry as zns, mgf2, and CaF2 (Daimon-20).",
